Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-12-2000||01:39 AM||||Well I got the 87 running. Now for the problems. I cant time it. I cant see any timing marks. It idling very rough. When its warmed up its at 1000ish rpm's. But its sputering bad at idel. How can I get my smoother idel back? When I hit the gas the sputering isnt as bad.<P>  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||4
Z||000001||GT Bastard||11-12-2000||03:30 AM||||If it's idling at 1000rpm, loosen the distributor and turn it clockwise just a bit! That will retard the timing a small amount.  Counterclockwise is advanced(faster idle.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||11-12-2000||03:34 AM||||Does that work for 88 4 bangers also?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-12-2000||02:03 PM||||Haze, Did you short out the ECM connector prior to checking timing? Also I usually look for the line with the engine off and mark it with chaulk. Makes it 1000 times easier to see it. I also know people who paint the line white.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||11-12-2000||03:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Haze, Did you short out the ECM connector prior to checking timing? Also I usually look for the line with the engine off and mark it with chaulk. Makes it 1000 times easier to see it. I also know people who paint the line white.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Short out the ECM connector prior to checking timing? Please explain.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <P>I can see the mark on the balancer, but it's an 1" or 2" away from the teeth marks.  <P>||||reg||5
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||11-12-2000||04:13 PM||||Haze,<P>Next!<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 11-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||11-12-2000||04:13 PM||||Haze,<P>Use the widest mark of the three, mark it in some way (I'm one of those guys who use paint!). Jumper pins A & B together of the diagnostic connector like you read codes. Set timming by averaging #1 cylinder and #4 cylinder to 10 degrees before TDC, shut off car, pull jumper and restart to notice the results.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||11-12-2000||04:22 PM||||1. Remove cover by lighter on center console<BR>2. Short out pins 1 and 2. (top left as you look at it)<BR>3. Start car<BR>4. Check/set timing<BR>5. shut off car<BR>6. remove shorting wire<BR>7. Start car.<BR>8. Drive car<BR>9. Enjoy!!||||reg||3
Z||000008||StuGood||11-12-2000||04:26 PM||||Yay!  Another paint user    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">! (I gotta get a life, huh?)<P>Okay -  just to clarify:  Remove the little trim panel (on the console, in the car) from around the cigarette lighter.  Requires a torx (T15)screwdriver.<P>The ALDL connector is under that trim panel.  Pins A & B (that you connect together, using a bent paper clip), are the two right next to each other in the bottom row (towards the floor mats  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">), all the way over on the passenger side of the car.  Connect A & B with the ignition off.   <P>Another way to get the same result, is to pull out the bigger of the two connectors on the base plate of the distributor.<P>When you restart the car, the ECM won't be messing with the ignition timing.  This lets you establish the basic timing (the 10 degrees BTDC), which is what you're trying to accomplish. <P>Hope I didn't tell you <B>too</B> many things you already knew   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.  Just thought a little clarification might be in order    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">        <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-12-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000009||ur2biteme||11-13-2000||06:17 AM||||87-88 4cyls use DIS.  no way to change timing on these, other than maybe changing/reprogramming the ecm?  ogre?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||11-13-2000||10:21 AM||||Haze's 87 is a V-6 SE. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||1
